  "_stockAuditsNote": "One record per distributor visit, backing the Stock Audit & Health page. Each line is an observation, not a count: `expected` freezes the system stock the visit saw, `conditionBreakdown` splits the physical stock four ways (good/nearExpiry/expired/damaged) and must reconcile to it, `storageBreakdown` records where it was found, and expiryDetails/disposition/damageType/evidence carry the exception detail. Records are terse — normalizeLine() in stock-audit.js fills in omitted buckets and derives `physical` from the condition sum. Line `status` distinguishes audited from not_found (not the same as zero). Audit `status` follows the lifecycle draft → in_progress → paused → review → completed, with cancelled/abandoned as exception states.",
